NAME
       mysql - the MariaDB / MySQL database client (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       mysql -h HOST -u USER -pPASSWORD [DATABASE] [-e "QUERY"]
       mysql -h HOST -u USER -p [DATABASE]

DESCRIPTION
       mysql connects to a database server (TCP port 3306) and runs queries,
       either from -e or at its MariaDB [db]> prompt (end each one with ;).

       Cyber Range's servers are a small pretend database. It understands:

           SHOW DATABASES;
           USE NAME;
           SHOW TABLES;
           DESCRIBE TABLE;
           SELECT * FROM TABLE;
           SELECT COL1, COL2 FROM TABLE WHERE COL = 'VALUE' LIMIT N;
           SELECT DATABASE();   SELECT USER();

       An account sees only the databases it was given.

OPTIONS
       -h HOST       the server (default localhost)
       -u USER       the database account
       -pPASSWORD    the password, written straight after -p (no space)
       -p            ask for the password
       -e "QUERY"    run the queries and leave

EXAMPLES
       mysql -h 10.10.20.40 -u webapp -pS3cret -e 'show databases'
       mysql -h 10.10.20.40 -u webapp -p shop

NOTES
       A password on the command line can be read by other users of the same
       machine (ps); -p alone asks for it instead.

SEE ALSO
       curl(1), nmap(1)
